    {
      "heading": "Carbon stores and flows",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Carbon is never made or destroyed. It just moves around."
        },
        {
          "say": "A place that holds carbon is a store. Here are three.",
          "write": "store (reservoir)",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 290,
            "alt": "Carbon cycle: atmosphere, living things and fossil fuels",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 200,
                "y": 20,
                "w": 160,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "teal",
                "label": "Atmosphere CO₂"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 30,
                "y": 200,
                "w": 140,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "green",
                "label": "Living things"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 390,
                "y": 200,
                "w": 150,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "grey",
                "label": "Fossil fuels"
              },
              {
                "kind": "arrow",
                "x": 190,
                "y": 70,
                "x2": 110,
                "y2": 195,
                "color": "green"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 80,
                "y": 120,
                "text": "photosynthesis",
                "size": 16,
                "color": "green",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Air, living things, oceans and rocks are all carbon stores."
        },
        {
          "say": "A process that moves carbon between stores is a flow.",
          "write": "flow (flux)"
        },
        {
          "say": "Plants swap carbon in days. Coal can lock it up for millions of years.",
          "write": "fast store vs slow store"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
