        },
        {
          "say": "Carbon dioxide also dissolves into the oceans, and some comes back out.",
          "write": "dissolving"
        },
        {
          "say": "Carbon passes along food chains. Volcanoes release carbon dioxide too."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Balancing combustion",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Let’s burn propane, the gas in barbecue bottles.",
          "write": "C₃H₈ + O₂ → CO₂ + H₂O"
        },
        {
          "say": "Three carbons on the left. So put 3 in front of CO two.",
          "write": "3CO₂"
        },
        {
          "say": "Eight hydrogens. So put 4 in front of water.",
          "write": "4H₂O"
        },
        {
          "say": "Oxygen last. Six plus four is ten atoms, so 5 O two.",
          "write": "5O₂"
        },
        {
          "say": "Now it balances.",
          "write": "C₃H₈ + 5O₂ → 3CO₂ + 4H₂O"
        }
      ]
    },
